<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stasioikos II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 312 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stasioikos II was the last king of Marion in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. In the wars of Alexander's successors he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a>, who in about 312 BCE took the city, razed it and moved its people to Paphos, ending the kingdom. Marion was later refounded as Arsinoe.</p></div>
